Applied verbatim from Droidspaces-OSS, which ships it as one of the two non-GKI
kernel patches every Droidspaces kernel is expected to carry:

  Documentation/resources/kernel-patches/non-GKI/
    02.fix_restore cgroup file prefix handling .patch
  https://github.com/ravindu644/Droidspaces-OSS

Why this device needs it
------------------------
Android mounts the v1 cpuset hierarchy with the `noprefix` flag. With that flag
the kernel names the files WITHOUT the subsystem prefix, so /dev/cpuset exposes
`cpus`, `mems`, `effective_cpus`, ... and NOT `cpuset.cpus` / `cpuset.mems`.
Anything speaking the standard cgroup v1 names - systemd, Docker, libcgroup,
Droidspaces - gets ENOENT.

Measured on saipan before this patch:

  none on /dev/cpuset type cgroup (rw,...,cpuset,noprefix,release_agent=...)
  ls /dev/cpuset/cpuset.cpus  ->  No such file or directory

Upstream makes the choice either/or in cgroup_file_name(). Droidspaces' patch
creates the prefixed name as an ADDITIONAL kernfs link when NOPREFIX is set, so
both spellings exist and nothing that worked before stops working.

The sibling patch 01.fix_kernel_panic_in_xt_qtaguid.patch is NOT applied: this
tree has no net/netfilter/xt_qtaguid.c, no CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_QTAGUID and
no qtaguid symbols in vmlinux. There is nothing to fix.

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
index 694b1cc8d..d0d04bff1 100755
--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
@@ -3496,6 +3496,11 @@ static int cgroup_add_file(struct cgroup_subsys_state *css, struct cgroup *cgrp,
 		spin_unlock_irq(&cgroup_file_kn_lock);
 	}
 
+	if (cft->ss && (cgrp->root->flags & CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX) && !(cft->flags & CFTYPE_NO_PREFIX)) {
+				snprintf(name, CGROUP_FILE_NAME_MAX, "%s.%s", cft->ss->name, cft->name);
+				kernfs_create_link(cgrp->kn, name, kn);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
